WEBVTT

00:29:28.147 --> 00:29:30.003
"Well, because I care about them."

00:29:30.027 --> 00:29:32.680
"OK, Doctor, let's start over."

00:29:32.704 --> 00:29:34.204
(Both laugh)

00:29:34.228 --> 00:29:36.156
AB: "Can you just try to say that?"

00:29:36.180 --> 00:29:38.324
AG: Oh, Adrienne, I love that,

00:29:38.348 --> 00:29:42.713
because if you go back
to the demand, control, support model,

00:29:42.737 --> 00:29:44.896
I think what I just heard

00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:49.578
is that by teaching physicians
to express empathy,

00:29:49.602 --> 00:29:52.216
you're actually helping them gain
a sense of control.

00:29:52.240 --> 00:29:57.056
That instead of having a stressful,
frustrating patient interaction,

00:29:57.080 --> 00:29:59.246
instead of dealing with lots of complaints

00:29:59.270 --> 00:30:02.726
and also feeling like
it's sort of out of their hands,